+- `find <bytes> -> <bytes>` is a patch without an address, as widescreen
+  patch lists give them ("initial value" and "change to"). When the game
+  starts, the app searches the disc's `default.xbe` sections for the first
+  bytes and turns every match (up to 64) into an `address: old -> new` patch.
+  Spaces between the hex pairs are free; `??` is a byte of any value (in the
+  second bytes: keep it as it is). Both must be the same length. A pattern that
+  matches nowhere (another release of the game) writes nothing; one that
+  matches more than 64 places too. Only in `[default.xbe]`.
+  ```
+  [default.xbe]
+  find DB442468 85C97D06 D805BC44 -> DB442468 90909090 D80D7444
+  ```
 - `[$u\default.xbe]` starts the patches of the game's Xbox Live title
